			<div class="content" id="post-content-1595309">
									

<p>There's no way the Foundation can suppress knowledge of the books' existence entirely. They can't possibly track down every copy sitting on the shelf in a public library, or at a yard sale, or swap meet, or what have you. What they can do is keep the books out of print and buy up copies that might end up on Amazon or eBay or so forth.</p>
<p>Really, the main difficulty for long-term containment (assuming any of the vintage toys are still floating around in the wild by then) is going to come in 2043, when the copyrights on the books expire.</p>

